@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: REQUIREMENT SHEET — the bar a def must clear to count as working, and which declared images no suite reaches
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
' covers: e2e/idle_test.go
' covers: defs/*/harness.manifest
' The sibling that owns the COMMANDS and where each half runs: release-gate.puml
'   (same directory). This file owns the BAR and the COVERAGE; that one owns the
'   procedure. Keeping them apart is deliberate — a bar that moves with a script
'   is not a bar.
' Moved here from _spec/_plans/ on 2026-09-10: what remained after its blockers
' closed is a standing requirement, not a plan.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── R1 · THE BAR ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' "Working" is not "it launched once for me". A def is GREEN when EVERY LADDER
' RUNG HOLDS on the sbx backend:
'
'   PROVEO_LADDER_TEST=1 PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET=<def> \
'     go test -tags e2e ./e2e/ -run Ladder -v
'
' PER DEF, not one climb — claudecode is the default target, so a bare run
' measures only it. The ladder is the right instrument because a rung failure
' NAMES ITS LAYER: "not green" arrives with an address rather than a symptom.
'
' ── R2 · A DOCKER+EGRESS RESULT DOES NOT SATISFY R1 ────────────────────────
' Every failure reported against this bar has been on sbx, and the fallback path
' has passed while sbx died. A sweep on docker answers a question nobody asked,
' and reporting it as coverage is how a red release goes out green.
'
' This is not a statement about the docker backend's worth. It is a statement
' about which measurement counts for THIS bar.
'
' ── R3 · IDLE IS COMPLEMENTARY, AND IS NOT THE GATE ────────────────────────
' `e2e/idle_test.go` asks a different question — does the assembled run survive
' being left alone — and NEITHER TEST IMPLIES THE OTHER. Both directions have
' been observed:
'   opencode   passed every rung while its idle behaviour was unverified
'   cursor     passed idle long before its ladder was ever climbed
' Worth running. Not what blocks a release.
'
' ── R4 · COVERAGE: EIGHT IMAGES DECLARED, FIVE REACHED ─────────────────────
' Four defs declare eight images between them, and the suites touch five. The
' two that matter are named rather than left to inference:
'
'   claudecode-solidity   no suite touches it. It builds FROM the claudecode
'                         image, so it inherits that layer's verdict — but the
'                         solidity toolchain on top is UNMEASURED, and
'                         inheritance is not a test.
'   cecli-browser         does not exist, so the ladder skips its browser rung.
'                         Whether that is deliberate is not recorded anywhere,
'                         and cecli may simply not want one.
'
' ── R5 · A SKIP MUST SAY WHICH KIND OF SKIP IT IS ──────────────────────────
' "Absent by design" and "we forgot" are INDISTINGUISHABLE in test output, and
' this has cost real accuracy twice already — release-gate.puml records
' `ladder-all` misreading the ladder verdict in both directions, once certifying
' four climbs that never happened and once reporting a def that passed every
' rung as not-run.
'
' So a skip is only acceptable when the reason is recorded where the reader
' lands: cecli-browser's absence belongs in cecli's manifest or in this sheet,
' not in the silence of a green run.
'
' ── WHAT THIS SHEET NO LONGER TRACKS, AND WHERE IT WENT ────────────────────
' Both of the blockers this file was opened for have closed, and keeping their
' investigations here would make a requirement sheet read as an open wound.
'
'   cecli ladder rung 2, ENOEXEC on the venv entry point
'     SUPERSEDED, structurally. That rung only exists for a def with no agent of
'     its own: `shellAgentTarget()` is `BuiltinAgent == "" && !DeclaresOwnAgent`,
'     and with the agent kit defaulted on cecli DECLARES ITS OWN AGENT — so the
'     `2-agent-command` rung is never generated for it. The launch defect it
'     chased is recorded in _spec/internal/sbx/shell-agent-launch.puml, and
'     _spec/_experiments/sbx-kit-capabilities.puml holds the climb where every
'     cecli rung held.
'
'   internal/ptyproxy PTY tests failing ~1 run in 3
'     FIXED, and re-measured before removal. The old note said they "do not
'     survive -count=2 at all"; `go test ./internal/ptyproxy/ -count=3` is now
'     green in under four seconds. The cause and the fix are in the commit that
'     drained the child's last output before closing the PTY master.
'
' A resolved blocker is deleted from a requirement sheet and kept in the spec
' that explains it. That is the difference between this file and the plan it
' used to be.
title Requirement sheet — what "all defs green" means,\nand the three images nobody measures

card "**R1 · THE BAR**\nevery ladder rung holds, on sbx, PER DEF" as BAR <<host>>
component "claudecode" as CC <<app>>
component "cursor" as CU <<app>>
component "opencode" as OC <<app>>
component "cecli" as CE <<app>>

component "**R2** a docker+egress pass\nis not a result for this bar" as R2 <<error>>
component "**R3** idle: complementary,\nnever the gate" as R3 <<app>>
component "**R4** claudecode-solidity\nunmeasured · cecli-browser absent" as R4 <<error>>
component "**R5** a skip that does not say\nWHICH kind it is" as R5 <<error>>

BAR ARROW_MAIN CC
BAR ARROW_MAIN CU
BAR ARROW_MAIN OC
BAR ARROW_MAIN CE
R2 ARROW_ERROR BAR : answers a question\nnobody asked
R3 ARROW_OPTIONAL BAR : run it; it does not block
BAR ARROW_ERROR R4
R4 ARROW_ERROR R5 : an absence and an oversight\nlook identical

note bottom of BAR
  **A rung failure names its layer.** That is why
  the ladder is the instrument and not a smoke
  test: "not green" arrives with an address. And
  PER DEF — claudecode is the default target, so
  a bare run measures one of four.
end note

note bottom of R2
  **Not a judgement on the backend.** Every
  failure against this bar has been on sbx, and
  the fallback passed while sbx died. It is about
  which measurement counts here, and reporting
  the other one as coverage ships a red release.
end note

note bottom of R3
  **Neither test implies the other**, observed in
  both directions: opencode passed every rung
  with idle unverified, and cursor passed idle
  long before its ladder was climbed.
end note

note bottom of R5
  **This has cost accuracy twice.** release-gate
  records ""ladder-all"" misreading the verdict
  both ways — certifying four climbs that never
  ran, then calling a def that passed every rung
  not-run. A silent skip is not a result.
end note

legend bottom
  **How to read this sheet**
  ==
  **R1 is the bar and it is per def**: every ladder rung, on sbx. R2 says a docker+egress
  pass is not a result for it. R3 keeps idle as a useful, non-blocking companion. R4 names
  the images no suite reaches, and R5 requires a skip to declare which kind it is.
  --
  **The commands live next door.** ""release-gate\.puml"" owns the procedure and the split
  between what runs in a sandbox and what needs a host. A bar that moves whenever a script
  changes is not a bar, which is why the two are separate files.
  ==
  **Both original blockers are closed and were deleted rather than archived here**: cecli's
  rung-2 ENOEXEC is structurally gone (it declares its own agent, so that rung is never
  generated), and the ptyproxy flake is fixed and re-measured green at ""-count=3"".
  --
  **Still unrecorded**: whether ""cecli-browser"" is absent by design. Until someone writes
  that down, its skip means nothing either way — which is exactly what R5 forbids.
end legend
@enduml
